d  searching  what you doing adrian come  adrian come  it takes three runs before they come  back with a single gun  with no help apparently coming they  began packing themselves into the  vehicles left at the lodge  the aim was to head out in a convoy  adrian would drive one car  it's gonna be the driver of your life  bro  within minutes they'd been ambushed  several drivers and vehicles were hit  and careered off the road  the brothers vehicle was amongst those  who kept going only to be ambushed a  second time  he just started shouting that he's hit  he's hit  and that his leg is off and he can't  drive  someone needs to take over everyone was  shouting at him just keep driving as far  as you can  he's like i'm trying a kilometer after  that  um he was you know just say i can't i'm  going guys i'm going  i was holding his shoulder over the  bullet went  trying to stop the blood and i was just  pumping out  ah started to drop and i was just  shouting back at them  to to put the other the other doses  inside  the the bullet the the gunshot wounds  and um was he still talking  no he had stopped talking about that  time and i was just shouting  that i love him and that i look after  his family  and that i'm so sorry i'm so sorry that  this has happened to  they hid in the forest until the next  day before dag helicopters rescued them  with wares insisting they take his  brother's body with them  this is the short shirt i was wearing  this is his blood  this is all of his blood that was on us  from  myanmar trying to save his life  people forget that we did  everything for everybody and it felt  like nobody was doing anything for us  and my brother paid the ultimate price  they just abandoned us didn't help us  no i'm left with this  adrian leaves behind a wife and three  young children  the amarillo lodge where he took refuge  was ransacked  with villagers saying 12 foreigners  who'd stayed behind  were beheaded here they buried them  beneath this tree  the militants